From fcf7b03c0c7fa8d92d8816a257c77451781615af Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christian Hewitt <christianshewitt@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 15:17:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 147/177] drm/meson: offer 10-bit deep color on GXM

GXM was refused deep color along with the rest of the GX family, on the
grounds that the clock code would program a dead PLL.  With the GXL/GXM
PLL parameters in place that is no longer true, and GXM is the one GX
part where the depth is real: S912 has a 10-bit pipeline and the 12-to-
10-bit dithering to feed it, where S905 and S905X have an 8-to-10
converter sitting in front of the HDMI controller and 8 bits behind it.

So offer 10 bits on GXM and keep 12 for the G12A family, whose pipeline
carries them.  A 12-bit wire on GXM would be dithered back down to 10
for the sake of a 1.5x TMDS rate.

GXBB and GXL are unchanged: a deeper wire format there would carry
upconverted 8-bit data at a higher clock, which buys nothing and puts a
working modeset at risk.

Untested on GXM hardware.  The clock tree entries are SoC-independent,
so this changes what a DC_30 sink is offered at 1080p24/25/30,
1080p50/60 and 4K24/25/30 on GXM from 8 to 10 bits.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5
Signed-off-by: Christian Hewitt <christianshewitt@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/meson/meson_encoder_hdmi.c | 17 ++++++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/meson/meson_encoder_hdmi.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/meson/meson_encoder_hdmi.c
index cd2815d851ad..5ff676a78959 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/meson/meson_encoder_hdmi.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/meson/meson_encoder_hdmi.c
@@ -393,11 +393,22 @@ meson_encoder_hdmi_get_inp_bus_fmts(struct drm_bridge *bridge,
 		return NULL;
 
 	/*
-	 * Deep color is implemented (PLL m/frac cases, analog band
-	 * parameters, VPU dither block) for G12A-family only; on older
-	 * SoCs the clock code would program a dead PLL.
+	 * Deep color needs PLL parameters for the deeper VCOs, which exist
+	 * for the G12A family and for GXL/GXM, and a pipeline with the bits
+	 * to carry, which is where the parts differ: S912 (GXM) is 10-bit
+	 * throughout and dithers 12 down to it, while S905 and S905X have
+	 * an 8-to-10 converter in front of the HDMI controller and nothing
+	 * behind it - a deeper wire format there carries upconverted 8-bit
+	 * data at a higher clock, which is worth nothing and risks the
+	 * modeset.  So: 10 and 12 bits on G12A-family, 10 bits on GXM,
+	 * 8 bits everywhere else.
 	 */
 	if (meson_encoder_hdmi_fmt_depth(output_fmt) > 8 &&
+	    !meson_vpu_is_compatible(encoder_hdmi->priv, VPU_COMPATIBLE_G12A) &&
+	    !meson_vpu_is_compatible(encoder_hdmi->priv, VPU_COMPATIBLE_GXM))
+		return NULL;
+
+	if (meson_encoder_hdmi_fmt_depth(output_fmt) > 10 &&
 	    !meson_vpu_is_compatible(encoder_hdmi->priv, VPU_COMPATIBLE_G12A))
 		return NULL;
 
